
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

<title>Enterprise Automation Scheduling & Webhook Data Routing</title>

<style>
:root {
    --background: #09090b;
    --surface: #101217;
    --surface-light: #161922;
    --border: #272a32;
    --cyan: #22d3ee;
    --violet: #7658A6;
    --text-primary: #f4f4f5;
    --text-secondary: #a1a1aa;
    --text-muted: #71717a;
    --success: #22c55e;
    --warning: #f59e0b;
    --danger: #ef4444;
    --radius: 10px;
    --transition: 0.25s ease;
}

* {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

html {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
}

body {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background:
        radial-gradient(
            circle at top right,
            rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.045),
            transparent 32%
        ),
        var(--background);

    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system,
        BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.7;
}

.container {
    width: min(1200px, calc(100% - 2.5rem));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 0 6rem;
}

/* HEADER */

.document-header {
    padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
}

.eyebrow,
.section-label {
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
}

h1 {
    max-width: 1000px;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

.subtitle {
    color: var(--violet);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
}

.overview {
    max-width: 900px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
}

/* METADATA */

.metadata {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
}

.metadata-item {
    padding: 0.5rem 0.85rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
}

.metadata-item strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
}

/* GENERAL SECTIONS */

section {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
}

h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.15rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}

h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
}

p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
}

.section-intro {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
}

/* DATAFLOW DIAGRAM */

.dataflow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0;
}

.flow-node {
    width: min(100%, 700px);
    padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    text-align: center;
    transition: var(--transition);
}

.flow-node:hover {
    border-color: var(--cyan);
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    box-shadow: 0 0 22px rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.08);
}

.flow-node h3 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
}

.flow-node p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
}

.flow-node.primary {
    border-color: var(--violet);
}

.flow-node.terminal {
    border-color: var(--cyan);
}

.flow-number {
    display: block;
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
}

.flow-arrow {
    height: 45px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
}

.flow-arrow span {
    width: 1px;
    height: 18px;
    background: var(--cyan);
}

.flow-arrow strong {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
}

/* ROUTING BRANCHES */

.routing-branches {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
}

.branch {
    padding: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--surface-light);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
}

.branch h3 {
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
}

.branch p {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
}

/* SPECIFICATION CARDS */

.specification-card {
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    transition: var(--transition);
}

.specification-card:hover {
    border-color: #3b4655;
}

.specification-header {
    padding-bottom: 1.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}

.specification-number {
    display: block;
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.specification-header h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
}

/* TECHNICAL LISTS */

.technical-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
}

.technical-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.85rem 0 0.85rem 1.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(39, 42, 50, 0.7);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
}

.technical-list li::before {
    content: "▹";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--cyan);
}

.technical-list strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
}

/* CALLOUTS */

.technical-callout {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--surface-light);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--violet);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
}

.technical-callout strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.technical-callout p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
}

code {
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-family: "SFMono-Regular", Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.88em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

/* INTEGRATION MAPPING */

.mapping-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
}

.mapping-card {
    padding: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--surface-light);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
}

.mapping-card .field {
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.mapping-card p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
}

/* FAULT MONITORING */

.fault-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
}

.fault-card {
    padding: 1.3rem;
    background: var(--surface-light);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    transition: var(--transition);
}

.fault-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: var(--cyan);
}

.fault-status {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.1);
    color: var(--danger);
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
}

.fault-card h3 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
}

.fault-card p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
}

/* TECHNOLOGY TAGS */

.stack-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
}

.stack-tag {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.7rem;
    background: rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
}

/* FOOTER */

footer {
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-align: center;
}

/* RESPONSIVE */

@media (max-width: 700px) {
    .container {
        width: calc(100% - 2rem);
        padding-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .specification-card {
        padding: 1.25rem;
    }

    .routing-branches {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .flow-node {
        padding: 1rem;
    }
}

/* PRINT */

@media print {
    body {
        background: white;
        color: #111;
    }

    .specification-card,
    .flow-node,
    .branch,
    .fault-card {
        background: white;
        border: 1px solid #ccc;
        break-inside: avoid;
    }

    p,
    .technical-list li {
        color: #333;
    }

    .container {
        width: 100%;
        padding: 1rem;
    }
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<main class="container">

    <!-- DOCUMENT HEADER -->

    <header class="document-header">

        <p class="eyebrow">
            ENTERPRISE AUTOMATION // CLOUD INTEGRATION
        </p>

        <h1>
            Enterprise Automation Scheduling &amp; Webhook Data Routing
        </h1>

        <p class="subtitle">
            Cloud Integration Architecture &amp;
            System Interaction Matrix
        </p>

        <p class="overview">
            A decoupled cloud integration architecture designed to
            coordinate scheduled upstream exports, intercept and
            normalize multi-source webhook payloads, route structured
            data through secure REST boundaries, and protect downstream
            relational systems through automated exception handling
            and forensic monitoring.
        </p>

        <div class="metadata">
            <span class="metadata-item">
                <strong>Status:</strong> Production Active / Highly Resilient Cloud Core
            </span>

            <span class="metadata-item">
                <strong>Architect:</strong> Angelique Greyling
            </span>

            <span class="metadata-item">
                <strong>Scale:</strong> Multi-Source Payload Router
            </span>

            <span class="metadata-item">
                <strong>Latency Profile:</strong> Sub-Second Target
            </span>
        </div>

    </header>


    <!-- ENTERPRISE DATAFLOW MAP -->

    <section>

        <p class="section-label">
            SYSTEM MAP // ENTERPRISE DATAFLOW
        </p>

        <h2>Cloud Integration &amp; Routing Architecture</h2>

        <p class="section-intro">
            The integration perimeter separates scheduled source exports
            from downstream database execution. Middleware acts as the
            orchestration and transformation boundary between external
            event notifications and internal relational data contracts.
        </p>

        <div class="dataflow">

            <div class="flow-node">
                <span class="flow-number">SOURCE LAYER // 01</span>
                <h3>UPSTREAM EXPORTS</h3>
                <p>Automated CSV blobs and transactional export events</p>
            </div>

            <div class="flow-arrow">
                <span></span>
                <strong>▼</strong>
            </div>

            <div class="flow-node primary">
                <span class="flow-number">SCHEDULING LAYER // 02</span>
                <h3>ZAPIER SCHEDULER</h3>
                <p>Scheduled trigger orchestration and controlled polling gate</p>
            </div>

            <div class="flow-arrow">
                <span></span>
                <strong>▼</strong>
            </div>

            <div class="flow-node">
                <span class="flow-number">MIDDLEWARE LAYER // 03</span>
                <h3>MIDDLEWARE ROUTER</h3>
                <p>Payload interception, field normalization and routing logic</p>
            </div>

            <div class="routing-branches">

                <article class="branch">
                    <h3>REST ENDPOINTS</h3>
                    <p>Webhook drops and outbound HTTP communication</p>
                </article>

                <article class="branch">
                    <h3>BUFFER PROCESSING</h3>
                    <p>Base64 decoding and payload partitioning</p>
                </article>

                <article class="branch">
                    <h3>STAGE 1 INTAKE</h3>
                    <p>Schema validation and parameter boundary checks</p>
                </article>

            </div>

            <div class="flow-arrow">
                <span></span>
                <strong>▼</strong>
            </div>

            <div class="flow-node terminal">
                <span class="flow-number">TARGET LAYER // 04</span>
                <h3>PRODUCTION ENGINES</h3>
                <p>SQL ingestion, relational overwrites and B-Tree index optimization</p>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="stack-tags">
            <span class="stack-tag">Zapier</span>
            <span class="stack-tag">Webhooks</span>
            <span class="stack-tag">REST API</span>
            <span class="stack-tag">JSON</span>
            <span class="stack-tag">Base64</span>
            <span class="stack-tag">PostgreSQL</span>
            <span class="stack-tag">SQL</span>
            <span class="stack-tag">SHA-256</span>
        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- STAGE 1 -->

    <section class="specification-card">

        <div class="specification-header">
            <span class="specification-number">
                STAGE 01 // WEBHOOK INGESTION
            </span>

            <h2>
                Webhook Ingestion Perimeter &amp; Trigger Tuning
            </h2>
        </div>

        <h3>1. Inbound Ingestion Logic</h3>

        <p>
            The event-driven pipeline initializes through an automated
            daily ingestion trigger. Rather than exposing standard
            open APIs to uncontrolled external connections,
            transaction notifications are routed through a secure,
            encrypted Zapier Webhook Listener Gateway.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            2. Payload Interception Specifications
        </h3>

        <ul class="technical-list">

            <li>
                <strong>Catch Webhook Action:</strong>
                The pipeline listens on a unique, obfuscated SSL endpoint.
                Upstream systems push notification payloads upon file
                export compilation events.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>Header Authentication Validation:</strong>
                Inbound packets are inspected for expected corporate
                security tokens before payload parsing begins.
                Invalid or corrupt metadata configurations trigger
                boundary rejection.
            </li>

        </ul>

        <div class="technical-callout">
            <strong>Perimeter Security Principle</strong>
            <p>
                Authentication and metadata validation occur before
                downstream transformation or database operations.
                This creates an explicit trust boundary between
                external notification sources and internal processing.
            </p>
        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- STAGE 2 -->

    <section class="specification-card">

        <div class="specification-header">
            <span class="specification-number">
                STAGE 02 // MIDDLEWARE TRANSFORMATION
            </span>

            <h2>
                Middleware Flattening &amp; Base64 Buffer Conversion
            </h2>
        </div>

        <h3>1. Data Type Normalization</h3>

        <p>
            Raw tracking payloads may contain binary attachments
            or complex nested multi-select parameters. To reduce
            unnecessary transfer overhead and prevent relational
            table blocking, Zapier operates as a lightweight
            orchestration and transformation router.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            2. Technical Execution Mechanics
        </h3>

        <ul class="technical-list">

            <li>
                <strong>Buffer Stream Partitioning:</strong>
                JSON bodies containing large text parameters or
                multi-byte character lists are separated into
                isolated field records and clean key-value pairs.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>Attachment Pointer Extraction:</strong>
                Rather than transferring large binary objects across
                web networks, the pipeline extracts the secure cloud
                destination URL and maps it as a text attribute.
                This maintains the specified payload-size target
                below 50KB.
            </li>

        </ul>

        <div class="technical-callout">
            <strong>Payload Optimization Strategy</strong>
            <p>
                Binary data and transactional metadata follow separate
                transfer paths. Reference pointers are passed through
                the integration layer instead of repeatedly transferring
                the underlying attachment objects.
            </p>
        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- STAGE 3 -->

    <section class="specification-card">

        <div class="specification-header">
            <span class="specification-number">
                STAGE 03 // REST DATABASE INGESTION
            </span>

            <h2>
                REST Target Gateway Ingestion &amp; schema.sql Dispatch
            </h2>
        </div>

        <h3>1. Relational Mapping Mechanics</h3>

        <p>
            Once the incoming data contracts have been flattened
            and normalized, Zapier issues an automated outbound
            REST API POST request to communicate with the downstream
            data-lake architecture boundaries.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            2. Enterprise Schema Alignment
        </h3>

        <p>
            Incoming fields are mapped against the PostgreSQL
            operational framework tables through defined
            relational insertion contracts.
        </p>

        <div class="mapping-grid">

            <article class="mapping-card">
                <div class="field">employee_id</div>
                <p>
                    Maps against
                    <code>dim_employees(employee_id)</code>
                    to enforce employee master-directory
                    foreign-key validation.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="mapping-card">
                <div class="field">timestamp</div>
                <p>
                    Maps into <code>fact_time_logs</code>
                    using ISO-8601 formatted timestamp strings
                    with explicit timezone handling.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="mapping-card">
                <div class="field">is_system_issue_found</div>
                <p>
                    Maps into
                    <code>fact_asset_checklists</code>
                    as a validated boolean variable.
                </p>
            </article>

        </div>

        <div class="technical-callout">
            <strong>Relational Integrity Boundary</strong>
            <p>
                The staging intake layer validates incoming
                identifiers, data types and timestamp formats
                before allowing transactional records to reach
                their target relational tables.
            </p>
        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- STAGE 4 -->

    <section class="specification-card">

        <div class="specification-header">
            <span class="specification-number">
                STAGE 04 // COMPLIANCE &amp; RESILIENCY
            </span>

            <h2>
                Compliance Monitoring &amp; Audit Circuit-Breakers
            </h2>
        </div>

        <h3>1. Automated Exception Catching</h3>

        <p>
            The automation architecture incorporates a multi-tier
            error-handling mechanism to intercept integration
            failures before they propagate into downstream
            execution layers.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            2. Fault Isolation Matrices
        </h3>

        <div class="fault-grid">

            <article class="fault-card">
                <span class="fault-status">HTTP 4XX</span>
                <h3>Client Exceptions</h3>
                <p>
                    Invalid requests, rejected authentication
                    tokens or malformed data contracts
                    are isolated for investigation.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="fault-card">
                <span class="fault-status">HTTP 5XX</span>
                <h3>Server Exceptions</h3>
                <p>
                    Target database outages and downstream
                    execution failures trigger controlled
                    processing interruption.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="fault-card">
                <span class="fault-status">ALERT LOOP</span>
                <h3>Incident Notifications</h3>
                <p>
                    Out-of-bounds metrics trigger
                    high-priority webhook notifications
                    to the designated engineering team.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="fault-card">
                <span class="fault-status">SHA-256</span>
                <h3>Forensic Validation</h3>
                <p>
                    Failed batch fingerprints support
                    integrity verification and
                    point-in-time forensic investigation.
                </p>
            </article>

        </div>

        <div class="technical-callout">
            <strong>Fault Containment &amp; Recovery Principle</strong>
            <p>
                Failed execution batches are isolated rather than
                silently discarded. Error metadata, response codes
                and batch validation fingerprints provide a traceable
                record for subsequent investigation and controlled
                recovery.
            </p>
        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- CLOSING ARCHITECTURE SUMMARY -->

    <section>

        <p class="section-label">
            ARCHITECTURAL OUTCOME // SYSTEM RESILIENCY
        </p>

        <h2>Decoupled Integration &amp; Controlled Data Delivery</h2>

        <p class="section-intro">
            The architecture establishes a controlled integration
            boundary between scheduled upstream exports and
            production relational systems. Payload validation,
            middleware normalization, schema alignment and
            exception monitoring operate as distinct processing
            responsibilities.
        </p>

        <div class="mapping-grid">

            <article class="mapping-card">
                <div class="field">01 / ISOLATION</div>
                <p>
                    Controlled webhook entry points and
                    authenticated inbound notifications.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="mapping-card">
                <div class="field">02 / NORMALIZATION</div>
                <p>
                    Structured payload conversion and
                    lightweight attachment routing.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="mapping-card">
                <div class="field">03 / INTEGRITY</div>
                <p>
                    Validated relational mappings and
                    controlled database ingestion.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="mapping-card">
                <div class="field">04 / RESILIENCY</div>
                <p>
                    Exception interception, incident
                    notifications and forensic traceability.
                </p>
            </article>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- FOOTER -->

    <footer>
        ENTERPRISE AUTOMATION SCHEDULING &amp; WEBHOOK DATA ROUTING
        <br>
        CLOUD INTEGRATION ARCHITECTURE
        // ANGELIQUE GREYLING
    </footer>

</main>

</body>
</html>
